## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose. Commercial purposes are not permitted purposes.

## Commercial Purposes

A commercial purpose is any purpose other than a noncommercial purpose. A purpose that is not commercial is a noncommercial purpose.

Noncommercial purposes include:

- Personal use for personal purposes (e.g. homelabs, hobby setups, local workflows)

- Educational use by educational institutions or for learning

- Research use by researchers or for research

- Development, test, and other use to create new software, so long as the new software is not used for a commercial purpose

Commercial purposes include:

- Selling the software or any other product or service

- Charging for access to the software, for hosting the software, or for any other service related to the software

- Using the software to provide a product or service to paying customers

